>>
Rule 1 (index tensor must be int64/Long to avoid "Expected a long tensor for index")
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = 4
>>
Rule 2 (input and source dtypes must match to avoid "self and source expected to have the same dtype")
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 3 (shape agreement between index and source: 1D index; source is scalar or same-length vector)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ ((ndim(v_3) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)) ∨ (ndim(v_3) = 0))
>>
Rule 4 (when accumulate=True, require a numeric dtype for input so addition is defined)
{v_1 : tensor, v_4 : bool} |= if v_4 then 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 5 (determinism-safe usage: perform at most one update and do not accumulate to avoid nondeterministic behavior)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor, v_4 : bool} |= (ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 1 ∧ v_4 = false ∧ ((ndim(v_3) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_3) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, 0) = 1)))
